  "why": "The paper proposes DeepXplore, a whitebox testing framework that uses differential testing and neuron coverage to find erroneous behaviors in Deep Neural Networks (DNNs). The methodology is evaluated on a set of standard, pre-trained or custom-trained DNN models. The paper makes no mention of these target models being equipped with any safeguards, such as adversarial training, input sanitization, or adversarial example detectors. The core design of DeepXplore focuses on finding inputs that cause disagreements between different models (`differential testing`) and activating new neurons (`neuron coverage`). The failure oracle is defined as a behavioral difference between models, not the circumvention of a protective measure. Consequently, the system is not designed to bypass safeguards, nor does the paper present any experiments demonstrating a successful bypass of a known defense mechanism.",
